      "title": "plugin-task-ui-6 — Author docs",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Author docs: a docs/chrome-and-ui.md with detailed ViewNode examples (panel, complex table, modal with a form) + a short \"Plugins (upcoming)\" pointer in README.md. Must be clearly marked design / target Phase 9 — not yet available until the WASM runtime (plugin-08) ships.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26 — superseded by a documentation consolidation, not by writing the file this task\noriginally described.\n\nWHAT THE TASK ASKED FOR: a `docs/plugin-authoring.md` with ViewNode examples + a README pointer,\nmarked as design-only until the WASM runtime ships.\n\nWHAT WAS THERE: that file already existed and was complete (274 lines, all three examples). But an\naudit found its examples used a titled `Panel` and a `Label` variant that never existed in the\ncode, and it pointed readers at BACKLOG.md, which is stale.\n\nWHAT WAS DONE INSTEAD (user-directed): four documents were saying overlapping and contradicting\nthings about the same subject — `pluggable-chrome-plugin-plan.md` (1832 lines),\n`grid-ui-chrome-plan.md` (229), `docs/plugin-authoring.md` (274), and a `docs/declarative-ui.md`\nwritten earlier in the session. They are now ONE file:\n\n**`docs/chrome-and-ui.md`** — 1738 lines, three parts:\n- Part I — the declarative UI model, current, with corrected examples.\n- Part II — every architecture section from both plan files, transferred VERBATIM (a script did the\n  copying, so nothing was lost to summarising), each block headed with the planner ids that own it.\n- Part III — the old phase plan mapped to planner ids, a table of everything in Part II that is now\n  out of date, and the work found to be tracked nowhere.\n\nThe four originals are now 14-line pointer stubs kept only so links do not break; delete them once\nnothing references them. Every document that pointed at them was repointed: AGENTS.md, README.md,\nPLAN.md, BACKLOG.md, agents-communication-plan.md, docs/widgets.md, docs/widget-architecture.md,\ndocs/sidebar-provider-modes.md, docs/surface-compositor.md, plus 8 planner phase descriptions.\n\nRULES CHANGED IN PLACE (both were \"settled\" and are now reversed — recorded so they are not\nrestored): AGENTS.md line 721 and its SETTLED table, and the plan file's §2.6.1 rule C, all said\n\"styling is not a prop\". They now say the theme gives the default and code may override it with a\nstring.\n\nALSO REMOVED: the G1–G8 task list in grid-ui-chrome-plan.md §6. All eight items were built; only G7\never had a planner id (F004/P001).\n\nWORK FOUND WITH NO PLANNER ENTRY, NOW ADDED:\n- F004/P009 (gridui-08) — dragging a container between regions. `DragSurfaceId` has one variant,\n  `DockFrame` has no drag handle, `ChromeRegion` receives nothing.\n- F003/P018 (plugin-10) — binding and listing contributed actions. `ActionMeta.default_binding` and\n  `ActionCatalog::describe_all()` both exist and nothing reads either.\n\nCHECKED AND FOUND ALREADY BUILT (so no phase was created): the shared chrome state layer, plan\nPhase 2 — `heca/src/chrome/state.rs`, 1158 lines, `SharedChromeState` + `WorkspacesContainerState`.\n\nThe README pointer this task asked for still stands and now points at the consolidated file.",
